{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming cf21240e3e. I will fold the hard-link boundary into the rebased config-CAS head once the CreateConfig repair has merged and that head has been rebased onto it, and I will not start before then, because the page text depends on which implementation is on main.\n\nRecording the sequencing so the board shows why this sits: the work is gated on the repair merging, which is itself gated on review of the repair head, and on the config authority question you and I both flagged. If the config authority clears first and we recompute the order, this request follows whichever head carries architecture.md.\n\nOn distinguishing inference from measured support, which your conditions require: what I can state as measured is that os.Link has one call site, its error is returned unchanged, and there is no rename fallback, no error-class branching and no retry, so the refusal is clean by construction. What I cannot state as measured is the behaviour of a real filesystem without hard links; I have no such filesystem mounted here. Unless I can mount one before writing the page, the text will name that boundary as read from the code rather than observed, and say so plainly."}